THE MOST SERIOUS FAMILY IN THIS SWEEP, because its failure direction is REPORTS
SAFE rather than reports noise.

Every Phoenix/Plug row shipped under net_recv, and the rows' own notes admitted
both directions in one slot -- "read request / write response", "receive and
publish events". Two failures at once, and they are not symmetric:

  * net_recv is an auto-derived taint SOURCE, so each sender MINTED
    untrusted_input at a call that emits.
  * nothing here was a SINK, so a Phoenix application had NO EGRESS ROWS FOR ITS
    OWN RESPONSE PATH. A secret written into a response body or header could not
    be reported as leaving the process at all.

SPLIT BY DIRECTION. 26 rows move to net_send: Controller.{render, json, text,
html, redirect, send_resp, send_download, put_status}; Plug.Conn.{send_resp,
send_file, send_chunked, chunk, resp}; and the Channel / Endpoint broadcast
families. Four stay receives: Plug.Conn.{read_body, fetch_query_params,
fetch_cookies}.

THE RESPONSE HEADER BUILDERS ARE INCLUDED DELIBERATELY (put_resp_header,
put_resp_cookie, put_resp_content_type). `put_resp_header(conn, "x", secret)` is
the point at which the secret enters the response that will be transmitted, and
nothing carries taint from the conn struct to the eventual send -- so a sink at
the point the value ENTERS is what catches it. Same asymmetry as WI-lunav.

THE ROUTER DSL IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE. Phoenix.Router.{get, post, resources,
scope} declare where a request ARRIVES, and arrival has no call site to
catalogue -- the Django rule from WI-hikut and the JS createServer rule from
WI-dosov. Moving them would relocate the receive to nothing.

`Plug.Conn.halt` is dropped outright: it marks the connection halted and moves
no bytes in either direction.

MEASURED A/B, 2 Phoenix repos, per-arm cache, arms sequential, canary on the
Phoenix/Plug net_send row count (NEW 26 / OLD 0 -- the old arm has no Phoenix
egress surface whatsoever).

  net_recv chains   53 -> 14   (-39)
  net_send chains   20 -> 58   (+38)   phoenix-framework alone: 0 -> 18
  all 10 other boundaries      IDENTICAL

The -39/+38 is accounted for PRIMITIVE BY PRIMITIVE: the four genuine receives
stay, the nine senders move, and the one-row difference is `halt`.

THE FINDING THAT MATTERS IS ONE THE TOOL COULD NOT PREVIOUSLY MAKE. The standing
claim file prohibits only host_fs sinks, so it cannot see a network change at
all; run against a NETWORK claim, plausible's UNTRUSTED-NO-NETWORK goes
violated(4) -> violated(7), and the three new findings sink at
Phoenix.Controller.json -- untrusted input reaching an HTTP RESPONSE BODY, which
is precisely the path that was structurally invisible. HOSTSECRET-NO-NETWORK
holds at 13 as an in-run control (those reach the network through HTTP clients,
which were always rowed).

DIRECTION: unlike F1-F4 this change REPORTS MORE. It adds sinks; the removals it
does perform delete false sources. Both halves move away from the all-clear.

